    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d685">

                <pb facs="0960" n="834" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg834"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A 4 e/210: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Mayer</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-04-27T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 27,
                                1925—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>85. This Government believes that after the customs treaty comes into force
                    following its ratification by the French Government, it would be appropriate for
                    the Chinese Government to issue a call convening <pb facs="0961" n="835"
                        xml:id="pg835"/> the Special Tariff Conference. This Government would be
                    willing to accept the tentative date of September 1, provided that date is also
                    convenient for the other governments which signed or have adhered to the
                    treaty.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
